    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0271" n="239" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v11/pg239"/>

                <head>135. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Lebanon<anchor n="1" xml:id="d135-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-07-14T23:36:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 14,
                                1958—11:36 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>204. London for Barbour. Deptel 189.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d135-f2"/> President has issued orders for amphibious landing
                    by Marine battalion landing team at Beirut 1500 Beirut time tomorrow July
                    fifteen. No later than noon (that is at least three hours prior landing) you
                    should therefore inform Chamoun that
                    foregoing action being taken pursuant his request and that US Government expects
                    full cooperation Lebanese armed forces. In so informing Chamoun you should at your discretion base your
                    remarks on draft political directive, Deptel 4790,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d135-f3"
                    /> and other pertinent telegrams. If feasible you should also urge Chamoun take necessary steps to prevent
                    information being transmitted outside of Lebanon prior actual landing.</p>
                <p>If for any reason task force should be unable make exact deadline, task force
                    commander being instructed communicate any time change to you.</p>
                <pb facs="0272" n="240" xml:id="pg240"/>
                <p>Shortly before landings you should request Lebanese Government issue immediate
                    NOTAM closing Beirut Airport and, if considered necessary, declaring airspace
                    over Lebanon danger area until further notice.</p>
                <p>While we hope that US action will bring improvement general situation Lebanon,
                    assume you, in collaboration with appropriate military commander, will take such
                    further necessary evacuation action as local circumstances may require.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
